n harm or potential harm to patients due to the effectiveness of the pre-release controls. The incident aligns with requirements for design and development of devices automated with computer software (qmsr-820.10-c-design-development) and emphasizes the importance of a robust software lifecycle, including verification and validation (mdr-annexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle). The finding does not trigger an immediate field safety action or require escalation.", "recommendation": "NO_ACTION", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 1}, "final_report_sha256": "b28655a4ae7708e381b80c94f8f941f4a61b59730698b103575f49035d220c9b", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": [], "recommendation": "NO_ACTION", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0002", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0002_r1", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0002", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 1, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "advisory_complete", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T22:15:36.415409Z", "total_steps": 4, "trace_id": "ef0778bd-f6b1-4c0a-b87c-1e9dfc3b2e7a"}
